WEBVTT

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:29.760
Welcome back.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.400
Are you ready to do a fantastic picture with me?

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.490
You've got your palette ready, your easel set up,

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.440
big glass of tea right beside you?

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.410
Alright, we're gonna run the colors across the screen,

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.360
in case you didn't get 'em last week,

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.700
and just let you see all the colors

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.340
that we use on each series here.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.540
So, today I thought we'd do a picture that,

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.240
oh, let's do something that's got some snow and ice in it,

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:55.250
and do something that's quite cold.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.130
And this is a fun little picture to do,

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:59.270
and I think you'll enjoy it very much.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:00.000
And we're gonna use this

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.600
the almighty brush lot today.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.780
We'll take it and I'll show you how to work with it.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.980
So let's start out, and we'll take just a little bit,

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.270
let's use a little bit of Indian yellow.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.470
Just a tiny little touch, right on the corner

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:17.390
of the big brush, and let's put a sun in the sky.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.790
I like to do those.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:25.690
Very gently, make a little circle here, just like so.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:26.970
There we go.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.020
Now, I'm gonna use the other corner of the brush

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.000
and go into just a small,

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:34.520
a small, small amount of permanent red, small amount.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.000
This stuff is unbelievably strong, so.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.440
Now, I have yellow on one side of the brush

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:45.450
and red on the other, and making little X's here.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.790
And we got the red on the outside

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:50.000
and the yellow on the inside, there we go.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.700
Just working around, just like so.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:00.000
Little touch more of the permanent red, just bring this

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.270
Right up, there we go.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:13.640
Looks like an egg I cooked the other day.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.660
It's a good thing I took up painting instead of cooking

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.190
because my eggs don't come out too well.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:20.340
All right, now, I'm gonna go into

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.940
a little bit of Prussian blue,

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.080
a tiny bit of Prussian blue, and Van Dyke brown.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.240
And just mix 'em on the brush.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.710
You don't have to worry about mixing 'em all up on the palette.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.000
Just mix 'em on the brush.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.760
and go all the way out to the farthest edge.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.480
And we're still using these little X's.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.000
We begin filling this in.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.400
There, as we get farther and farther away from the sun,

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.520
we want it to get darker and darker.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:53.660
Just bring that right on out.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:58.650
Okay, now I'll clean the big brush.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.000
Once again, we clean the brushes

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.460
with odorless paint cleaner.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:10.520
And shake him off a little.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:12.820
That's the most fun of painting.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.500
All right, now, we're gonna take here

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.670
and just begin blending all this together.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.250
Just blend it, working from the lightest color outward,

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:24.920
always, just bring it together.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.000
And here we use quite a bit of pressure on the canvas.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.970
We're pushing this color into the canvas

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:30.000
and blending it together.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.360
Remember not to take this dirty brush

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.950
after you've hit this gray and come back into the center.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.960
Always work outward.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.300
Just bring it together.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.340
You don't want to be able to tell where one color stops

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:48.090
and the other one starts.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:53.020
Okay, nice even distribution of color.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:56.690
Very gently, I'll just go all the way across.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:01.930
all together.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:05.450
Now, let's build a happy little sun in the sky.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:08.970
And we'll do that using a one-inch brush

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.070
and titanium white.

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:15.430
And let's load a lot of paint into the bristles here.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:17.870
Go right into the center of this yellow color,

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:21.030
push very hard, and turn the brush.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:24.030
We're literally pushing this paint right into the canvas,

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.610
right into the fabric.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.730
There.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.000
And we can clean the brush.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:38.600
Now with a knife, we're gonna take off the excess paint

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:41.230
so we can blend it together.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.160
That's all there is to it.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:45.550
Now with a nice clean dry brush,

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:55.630
we can just begin bringing all this together.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:05:00.000
Okay, we just about have a pretty little

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.360
the sky done here already.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:10.430
Now, let's go right in to the Alizarin Crimson,

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.790
right into the Crimson,

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:16.640
and a tiny, tiny little touch of Prussian Blue.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.000
The Prussian Blue is at least 100 times stronger

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.160
than the Crimson.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.660
Tiny bit of Prussian Blue,

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.550
a lot of Crimson in comparison.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.870
Just a little, there we go.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.380
Load this brush full of paint.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.480
Now we're gonna put some basic tree shapes in there.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.600
So let's go right up here to the canvas.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.000
And we touch and bend the bristles.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.660
And that's what makes all the leaves and stuff happen here.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:43.570
Touch and bend the bristles.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:49.400
Turn the brush in the shape of the tree here.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.190
Isn't that something?

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:56.830
- I used to work for weeks to make a tree.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.580
- Man, maybe, maybe right here.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:06.410
But you see how hard we're striking the canvas.

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:11.290
We really wanna push this paint right into the fabric.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:17.350
It is a little one right there.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:18.970
And when you're doing this at home,

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:21.860
don't worry about following exactly what I'm doing.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.440
We're really trying to teach you a technique.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.370
We're not trying to teach you to copy.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:30.000
So let your imagination be your guide.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.890
Alizarin in blue, oh, right here.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:37.130
I see a big tree, there it is.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.310
So you just imagine things in your mind

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:45.420
and then put 'em on canvas.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:49.130
Now, we'll just come right on down here a little,

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:55.950
and we'll throw in some nice little areas here.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:07:00.000
Go, here, maybe there's a little bush

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:04.420
Once again, just let your imagination go crazy here

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:10.780
and do whatever feels right.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:14.660
Alright, now maybe while we have all this color on the brush,

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.620
let's imagine that there's a little pool of water down here.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.240
So, just pull straight down.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.420
It's most important that you pull straight down.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.320
This is gonna end up being the reflections in the water,

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:30.000
so pull it straight down.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.240
a little tiny bit more blue here, there.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:38.460
Make it a little darker so it looks a little deeper.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:45.750
And the blue will also make it look a little colder.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.060
There we go.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:53.640
Now, very gently, come across with the brush, very gently.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:55.000
Already that looks like water,

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.580
and you've done virtually nothing, there we go.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.270
Okay, now let's take the pallet knife,

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:07.210
and we'll use a little bit of Van Dyke brown here.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.200
Just straight Van Dyke brown.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.700
And let's put some happy little trunks in here.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:16.490
You touch the canvas, and pull it slightly to the side.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:26.630
Just slightly, and create almighty trunks, right up here.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:30.000
And trees don't always grow straight, let 'em bend.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:34.090
Maybe when they were little, a big moose came along

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:37.310
and stepped on 'em and put a little crook in 'em.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:40.100
Okay, here we go.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:42.400
I refer to moose 'cause I don't know if I've mentioned it,

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:44.520
but my home is in Fairbanks, Alaska,

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:50.250
so we see a lot of moose and caribou, elk,

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.910
all those good things.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.410
If you wanna make that one a little wider,

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:56.710
I decided it's a little closer,

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:59.300
so we'll make him a little bigger.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.000
Just make him a little bigger.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.410
Now, I'll use a little bit of the titanium white,

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.590
and let's highlight these trees.

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:10.410
Touch, and just give it a little pull.

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:14.020
And when you're doing this, let the knife sort of go around,

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:18.150
so it gives the appearance of roundness in the tree.

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:21.700
Just let it come around.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:26.490
And let's go over here and highlight this little tree.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.190
Don't want him to get upset,

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:29.570
'cause he don't have any highlight.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.950
Now, if this is our light source,

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:38.480
this tree's gonna be highlighted on the opposite side.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:41.540
So, we'll just come right here

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:45.750
and put a little highlight over here, like so.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:49.760
Okay, while we have this white on our palette,

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:53.920
let's take and begin laying in a little bit of snow here.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.260
Just lay this in.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:57.840
This is titanium white.

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:05.520
Gentle touch, touch.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:11.230
There you go.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:13.220
Maybe there's some snow all around the water here.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:16.610
Isn't that fantastic?

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:22.690
There's no big secret to this.

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:25.300
It's like anything else.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:28.390
You learn the technique, you practice it,

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:38.600
and master it very quickly.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.760
And we're not really looking for definite shapes right now.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:57.410
All we're doing is just laying a little snow in.

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:59.250
Let's take, begin.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.700
all these trees and bushes here.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.210
We use a one-inch brush, and back to our golden rule.

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:08.680
A thin paint will stick to a thick paint.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.740
So I've dipped the brush into some Magic White,

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.860
and then I'm gonna go through the Titanium White.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:16.730
All the Magic White does is thin this down,

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.090
so we can get it to stick to the thicker paint

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:21.940
that's on the canvas already.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:23.400
Load a lot of paint into the bristles.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:26.450
Probably the biggest mistake made when you first start

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.650
is you're stingy with paint.

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:30.000
You gotta load a lot of paint in there, so you don't have

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.400
hit so hard, all you have to do is barely touch the canvas

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.700
and bend the bristles a little bit.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:38.610
Okay, let's make all these snow-covered little things here.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.590
All you do is just barely touch the canvas

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:45.930
and just let 'em bend.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:49.370
Look at all of those things.

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:54.520
Just touch and let it bend.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:57.910
Here we go.

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:00.000
For so many years, I was a traditional painter.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:05.170
and I spent weeks trying to paint a picture.

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:08.520
Oh, the agony, I remembered.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:09.780
There, let's put some highlights

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:14.320
on this little bush right out here.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:19.590
Okay, let's go over to this little big tree here.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:25.150
There, and we'll add just a little bit more

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:26.790
of the Magic White to thin it.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.360
See, it's beginning to pick up the crimson.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:38.730
It's getting a nice warm pink glow.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:48.770
Paint, you got your winter coat out yet?

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:51.260
It's gonna get colder.

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:56.800
Let's put a happy little bush right there

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:58.740
and let these come right down onto the snow.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:03.570
Very important, do not kill all these darker areas

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:05.160
or all you'll have is a canvas that's white

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:07.460
and that's what we started with.

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:22.100
Here, shape it.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:24.320
I really hope you're painting with us at home

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.790
and enjoying this half as much as we are here.

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:33.000
Look there, we have one side almost completed already.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:37.010
We'll put some little snow covered bushes right over here.

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.120
Once again, don't kill all this dark.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:48.950
Alright, just jump right on there.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:55.890
There's another one right in here.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.520
Okay, let's do this great big ol' tree up here.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:06.990
Thin this paint down just a touch more.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:11.590
Go right up here.

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:16.850
Just begin producing thousands of little sparkles up here.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:24.460
Think how long that'd take you with your one-haired brush.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.950
Mm, okay.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.210
Now, let's take the pallet knife,

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:36.560
and this is just a clean knife with nothing on it,

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.940
and just scrape through the paint here and there,

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.460
just to make some little stems.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:54.990
There we go, some over in here.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.340
You know, it never stops to amaze me

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.410
as we travel around teaching this method,

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.820
I watch people who have never painted in only a day or two

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:06.620
produce a painting that just, they can't believe it.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.500
You see 'em, their eyes light up,

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:11.030
they become so excited, and they can do it,

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:12.710
and you can do it.

00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:17.140
All you need to do is pick up a brush and try.

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.450
Okay, a few little sticks here and there.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:22.100
There's some right there.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:26.550
Now, let's take, so we have some ragged edges along here

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:28.870
where I was putting the snow down to the water.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.000
So all you do is take your large

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.460
Grab a hold of it, pull it down.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.040
Let it become part of the reflection.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:37.230
It acts as a highlight in the reflection.

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:40.020
If you don't have enough, you can go right into the white

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:43.970
with the large brush, touch, and pull down.

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:50.590
Mmm, just wherever you want these little highlights

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:51.890
in the reflection.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:54.550
And then very gently, come across.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:57.060
Just enough to give it a watery feel.

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.840
You don't want to destroy all this.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:06.200
Okay, now, let's take a little bit of the magic white,

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:08.860
and when you're using this, pull it out very flat,

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:17.140
and come across, so we can make a very fine line here,

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:24.320
just like so, let's let it go.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:34.070
Let's bring that snow down just a tiny bit more.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:46.340
Just bring him right on down.

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:49.000
I like these kind of scenes because,

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.770
well, to be honest, I'm a nature freak.

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:55.660
I love to walk through the woods and talk to the animals.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:58.220
Don't tell anybody that.

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:00.000
I even talk to trees at times.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:04.150
But you need to understand nature

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:07.250
to appreciate the great, great things

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:09.810
that have been created.

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:12.560
We spend so much of our life walking around

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:15.800
looking with never, never, never seeing.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.880
And if painting teaches you nothing else,

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:19.120
it'll teach you to see nature,

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:21.220
to appreciate some of the beauty

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:25.220
that's around us every day that we take for granted.

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:28.100
All right, maybe we'll have, let's do this.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:29.960
Let's have snow come right down through here.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.110
There we go.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:38.680
Zoom.

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:40.020
And this should make you happy when you're doing it.

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:44.510
It should give you good feelings inside.

